# The server runs on Linux, so LF is the only line ending in the repository and
# in the working tree. Declaring it here makes checkouts identical on every
# machine instead of depending on each developer's core.autocrlf setting, which
# is what produces Git's "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets Git must never convert. Apple's root certificates and signing keys are
# byte-exact: a line-ending rewrite would break signature verification.
*.cer binary
*.p8 binary
*.pem binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
